asset:        Mosaic.wgsl
title:        GL Transitions "Mosaic" transition shader, hand-ported to WGSL
author:       Xaychru (ported to gl-transitions by gre) (upstream GLSL); FilmCraft contributors (WGSL port and Rust reference)
source:       https://github.com/gl-transitions/gl-transitions/blob/master/transitions/Mosaic.glsl
license:      MIT
license-file: crates/render/src/transitions/shader/LICENSE-gl-transitions.txt
added:        2026-10-17 by FilmCraft contributors (C1, lane T)
notes:        Hand port of the upstream GLSL to WGSL, keeping its Author/License header; the upstream header says License: MIT. The FilmCraft host (prelude.wgsl, original work) supplies the bindings, progress (eased on the CPU), getFromColor/getToColor (clamped bilinear, linear premultiplied colour, uv origin bottom left) and GLSL helpers. The Rust reference of the same function is in cpu.rs. Changes from upstream: the sin-based Rand() replaced by an integer cell hash, identical on CPU and GPU, except that the starting cell (0, 0) keeps upstream's value 0; the tile index is biased by 1/1000 of a tile so pixel centres exactly on a tile edge fall the same way on every GPU and the CPU.
